{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_3>\nimport sys\n\ndef compute():\n    MOD = 1000000007\n    T = 1\n    \n    for _ in range(T):\n        P, K = map(int, input().split())\n        \n        if K == 0:\n            print(pow(P, P - 1, MOD))\n            continue\n        \n        # Build functional graph: i -> (K*i) % P\n        next_node = [K * i % P for i in range(P)]\n        \n        # Track visited nodes and cycle lengths\n        visited = [False] * P\n        cycle_freq = {}\n        \n        for node in range(P):\n            if visited[node]:\n                continue\n            \n            # Trace the path until we find a visited node\n            path = []\n            cur = node\n            while not visited[cur]:\n                visited[cur] = True\n                path.append(cur)\n                cur = next_node[cur]\n            \n            # Find where the cycle starts\n            try:\n                idx = path.index(cur)\n                cycle = path[idx:]\n                cycle_len = len(cycle)\n            except ValueError:\n                cycle_len = 1\n            \n            cycle_freq[cycle_len] = cycle_freq.get(cycle_len, 0) + 1\n        \n        # Calculate final answer\n        result = 1\n        for length, freq in cycle_freq.items():\n            if length == 1:\n                exp = length * freq\n            else:\n                exp = length * freq + 1\n            result = (result * pow(exp, freq, MOD)) % MOD\n        \n        print(result)\n\ncompute()\n</your_rewritten_code_3>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final long MOD = 1000000007;\n    \n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String[] line = br.readLine().split(\" \");\n        int P = Integer.parseInt(line[0]);\n        int K = Integer.parseInt(line[1]);\n        \n        if (K == 0) {\n            System.out.println(powerMod(P, P - 1, MOD));\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        // Build functional graph: i -> (K*i) % P\n        int[] nextNode = new int[P];\n        for (int i = 0; i < P; i++) {\n            nextNode[i] = (K * i) % P;\n        }\n        \n        // Track visited nodes and cycle lengths\n        boolean[] visited = new boolean[P];\n        Map<Integer, Integer> cycleFreq = new HashMap<>();\n        \n        for (int node = 0; node < P; node++) {\n            if (visited[node]) {\n                continue;\n            }\n            \n            // Trace the path until we find a visited node\n            List<Integer> path = new ArrayList<>();\n            int cur = node;\n            while (!visited[cur]) {\n                visited[cur] = true;\n                path.add(cur);\n                cur = nextNode[cur];\n            }\n            \n            // Find where the cycle starts\n            int idx = -1;\n            for (int i = 0; i < path.size(); i++) {\n                if (path.get(i) == cur) {\n                    idx = i;\n                    break;\n                }\n            }\n            \n            int cycleLen;\n            if (idx == -1) {\n                cycleLen = 1;\n            } else {\n                cycleLen = path.size() - idx;\n            }\n            \n            cycleFreq.put(cycleLen, cycleFreq.getOrDefault(cycleLen, 0) + 1);\n        }\n        \n        // Calculate final answer\n        long result = 1;\n        for (Map.Entry<Integer, Integer> entry : cycleFreq.entrySet()) {\n            int length = entry.getKey();\n            int freq = entry.getValue();\n            long exp;\n            if (length == 1) {\n                exp = (long) length * freq;\n            } else {\n                exp = (long) length * freq + 1;\n            }\n            result = (result * powerMod(exp, freq, MOD)) % MOD;\n        }\n        \n        System.out.println(result);\n    }\n    \n    // Fast modular exponentiation\n    static long powerMod(long base, long exp, long mod) {\n        long result = 1;\n        base = base % mod;\n        while (exp > 0) {\n            if ((exp & 1) == 1) {\n                result = (result * base) % mod;\n            }\n            base = (base * base) % mod;\n            exp >>= 1;\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.0001394651480950415, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.00027164106722921133, -2.1934269170742482e-05, -0.018171969801187515, -0.6937263607978821, -0.00025459862081333995, -2.8371408916427754e-05, -0.0029950544703751802, -0.0008953376673161983, -0.00012766500003635883, -1.1324817933200393e-05, -6.258291978156194e-05, -0.023249173536896706, -0.004079354461282492, -0.050135936588048935, -0.00047052756417542696, -0.00036995718255639076, -4.887569048150908e-06, 0.0, -2.384185506